---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Aging at Home Lab | Practical Aging-in-Place Checklists" description="Practical checklists, home-safety guides, and caregiver organization systems for families helping older adults stay safer at home.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Practical aging-in-place help</p>
      <h1>Make aging at home feel less overwhelming.</h1>
      <p class="lede">Calm, practical checklists and caregiver tools for families helping older adults stay safer, more organized, and more supported at home.</p>
      <div class="button-row">
        <a class="button primary" href="/start-here/">Start with the checklist</a>
        <a class="button secondary" href="/guides/">Browse the guide library</a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="hero-card" aria-label="Aging at Home master checklist preview">
      <div class="checklist-card">
        <div class="checklist-top">
          <div>
            <div class="eyebrow">Core asset</div>
            <div class="checklist-title">Aging at Home Master Checklist</div>
          </div>
          <span class="status-pill">In review</span>
        </div>
        <div class="check-item"><span class="check-dot"></span><span>Clear walking paths and obvious trip hazards.</span></div>
        <div class="check-item"><span class="check-dot"></span><span>Check bathroom, bedroom, stairs, lighting, and entryways.</span></div>
        <div class="check-item"><span class="check-dot"></span><span>Organize medications, emergency contacts, and home access notes.</span></div>
        <div class="mini-note">Built for families who need a practical first pass before deciding what needs professional help.</div>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <section class="trust-row" aria-label="Editorial trust principles">
    <div class="trust-item">No fear-based selling.</div>
    <div class="trust-item">Clear professional-help triggers.</div>
    <div class="trust-item">Checklists before product pitches.</div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="guide-categories">
    <p class="eyebrow">Resource library</p>
    <h2 id="guide-categories">Built around the decisions families actually face.</h2>
    <p class="section-kicker">Each section is designed to become a practical library of guides, templates, diagrams, and product decision frameworks.</p>
    <div class="grid" aria-label="Core guide categories">
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon">01</div>
        <h3><a href="/start-here/">Start Here</a></h3>
        <p>First-weekend plans, aging-in-place checklists, and the first decisions families need after a fall, hospital stay, or safety concern.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon">02</div>
        <h3><a href="/home-safety/">Home Safety</a></h3>
        <p>Room-by-room checklists for bathrooms, bedrooms, kitchens, stairs, entries, lighting, and common fall-risk areas.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon">03</div>
        <h3><a href="/caregiver-organization/">Caregiver Organization</a></h3>
        <p>Binder pages, medication lists, emergency contacts, appointment notes, sibling coordination tools, and weekly care check-ins.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon">04</div>
        <h3><a href="/senior-tech/">Senior Tech</a></h3>
        <p>Plain-English decision guides for medical alerts, fall detection, privacy-safe monitoring, medication reminders, and caregiver apps.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon">05</div>
        <h3><a href="/home-modifications/">Home Modifications</a></h3>
        <p>Questions to ask before installing grab bars, ramps, stair lifts, shower changes, lighting upgrades, and accessibility improvements.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-icon">06</div>
        <h3><a href="/templates/">Templates</a></h3>
        <p>Printable worksheets for home safety, emergency contacts, medication lists, appointment notes, and family responsibilities.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="split-section">
    <div class="callout">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why this exists</p>
      <h2>For the moment when a family needs a next step.</h2>
      <p>Many families start searching after a fall, hospital stay, missed medication, or hard conversation about independence. Our job is to make the next step clearer without pretending a checklist replaces professional judgment.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <div class="card-icon">✓</div>
      <h3>Our publishing rule</h3>
      <p>Every major guide should include practical next steps, credible source support, and an original asset such as a checklist, worksheet, comparison table, or decision tree.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
